{"event_id": 5, "timestamp": "2026-11-15T18:55:17.648601+00:00", "run_id": "df4a3a71bd2a", "method": "direct", "type": "request_end", "request_id": "0f647aa69578", "agent_id": 0, "endpoint_index": 0, "stage": "code_propose", "latency_ms": 3109.13, "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 294, "completion_tokens": 306, "total_tokens": 600, "estimated": false}, "completion_tokens_charged": 306, "error": null, "response": "```python\ndef natural_sort_strings(strings):\n    \"\"\"Sort strings by natural order (ASCII-digit vs non-digit runs).\n\n    Args:\n        strings: list of str to sort.\n\n    Returns:\n        list of str sorted naturally; input order preserved for equal keys.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Helper: split a string into (kind, value) pairs.\n    # kind is 'digit' or 'text'. digit values are int, text values are str.\n    def _key(s):\n        runs = []\n        i = 0\n        n = len(s)\n        while i < n:\n            ch = s[i]\n            if ch.isascii() and ch.isdigit():\n                j = i\n                while j < n and s[j].isascii() and s[j].isdigit():\n                    j += 1\n                runs.append(('digit', int(s[i:j])))\n                i = j\n            else:\n                j = i\n                while j < n and not (s[j].isascii() and s[j].isdigit()):\n                    j += 1\n                runs.append(('text', s[i:j]))\n                i = j\n        return runs\n\n    # Decorate-sort-undecorate.\n    decorated = [( _key(s), idx, s) for idx, s in enumerate(strings)]\n    decorated.sort(key=lambda x: (x[0], x[1]))\n    return [s for _, _, s in decorated]\n```", "reasoning": null, "finish_reason": "stop", "puzzle_id": "eva-natural_sort_strings", "node_id": "code-root-eva-natural_sort_strings", "round": 0}
